## KRAFTWERK - POCKET CALCULATOR (TASCHENRECHNER)
#  Full Arrangement Cover for PULP / SKRED. 126 BPM, A major, 88 bars (~2:47).
#  Written & Produced by Ralf Hütter, Florian Schneider, Karl Bartos (1981).
#  From the seminal electronic album 'Computer World' (Computerwelt).
#  Self-contained: 100% synthesized analog electronic percussion (pitch-drop sine kick,
#  bitcrushed noise snap snare, micro-tick synthetic hats), Casio VL-80 calculator bleeps,
#  Minimoog octave motorik bass, and authentic A major melodies.
#  All patterns strictly pinned to exact bar boundaries (x15, x31, x63).
#  Load:   [pocket-calc.sk] /ls
#  Start:  play        Stop:  stop
#
#  VOICE MAP (all labeled via [name] vt):
#    v0  electronic sine kick (w0 pitch drop) + v5 transient click (w5)
#    v1  noise snap snare (w5 bitcrushed bc4) + v4 analog tone body (w1)
#    v2  synthetic micro-tick hat (w5)  v3  electronic open hat sizzle (w5)
#    v6  Minimoog motorik bass saw (w1) + v7 sub pulse oct (w2)
#    v8  Kraftwerk lead synth (w2 pulse) + v9 detuned saw partner (w1)
#    v13 Casio VL-80 calculator bleep (w1 pure square)
#
#  DELAY BUSES:
#    Bus 1: Clean slapback echo for Casio calculator bleeps (16th note, 126 BPM)
#    Bus 2: Stereo tape echo for Kraftwerk lead synth (dotted eighth, 126 BPM)
# ======================================================================

[KRAFTWERK - POCKET CALCULATOR] puts
M 126 16

## DELAY BUSES
# Bus 1: Clean slapback echo for Casio VL-80 bleeps (16th note)
DS 1 126 .25
DL 1 - - 4 0 0 8
DD 1 7 2
DP 1 1

# Bus 2: Stereo tape echo for Kraftwerk lead synth (dotted eighth)
DS 2 126 .75
DL 2 - - 8 2 3 11
DD 2 6 3
DP 2 1

## VOICES
# Drums: 100% Pure Kraftwerk Synthesized Analog Percussion
# Electronic Kick: Pure sine wave with fast pitch drop (Minimoog style)
v0 w0 a8 p0 t.001,.14,0,.04 g0 n62 g.03 n33 [kraftwerk electronic kick] vt
v0 >5
v5 w5 a-5 p0 t.001,.012,0,.005 k3500 q1.5 [kick click] vt
v0 G5 H5

# Electronic Snare: Tight white noise snap with bitcrusher + analog tone body
v1 w5 a7 p0 t.001,.11,0,.03 j1 k2400 q3.5 bc4 r2 ds.15 [kraftwerk noise snare] vt
v1 >4
v4 w1 a-2 p0 t.001,.09,0,.02 n57 [snare body tone] vt
v1 G4 H4

# Micro-tick Hats: Pristine electronic click
v2 w5 a-5 p.25 t.001,.025,0,.005 k6500 q4.0 [electronic hat tick] vt
v3 w5 a-4 p-.25 t.001,.14,0,.04 k5500 q3.0 [electronic open sizzle] vt

# Minimoog Motorik Bass: Saw wave driven into resonant ladder filter + sub pulse
v6 w1 a4 p0 t.001,.14,.25,.06 j1 k1200 q2.6 r1 ds.15 [minimoog bass saw] vt
v6 >7
v7 w2 a1 N-12,0 p0 r0 [minimoog sub pulse] vt
v6 G7 H7

# Ralf Hütter Lead Synth: Warm analog pulse/saw lead
v8 w2 a-1 p0 t.004,.32,.45,.12 j1 k2200 q1.6 r2 ds.25 [kraftwerk lead synth] vt
v8 >9
v9 w1 a-5 N0,6 p.35 r0 [kraftwerk lead detune] vt
v8 G9 H9

# Casio VL-Tone / VL-80 Handheld Calculator: Pure square wave bleeps
v13 w1 a-3 p0 t.001,.08,0,.02 j0 k4500 q.7 r1 ds.20 [casio vl-80 beep] vt

## EVENTS
[O DQ] /ceb 4 99
/cer 1

## STREAMS
